  "number": "9.3",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Let be a field of characteristic different from two, and let on have rank one with monodromy . For , one has Thus tensoring global sections does not give the global sections of the tensor product.   A global section is an invariant vector, hence satisfies and vanishes. The tensor product has monodromy . The resulting section map has zero source and target . Both statements follow from the local-system constructions and circle calculation in Note I, Chapter 10 .  "
