  "title": "",
  "body": " Étale morphism Standard étale algebra  A morphism of schemes is étale if it is flat, locally of finite presentation, and unramified. Equivalently, it is smooth of relative dimension zero. These scheme-theoretic conditions are understood in their usual local sense. A basic algebraic model is a standard étale algebra  where is monic and its derivative is invertible in .  "
