  "id": "st-c13-root-cover",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "st-c13.html#st-c13-root-cover",
  "type": "Example",
  "number": "13.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": " Let be an integer invertible in the field . The map is finite étale and surjective. In characteristic , the analogous map is not étale.  The target algebra adjoins a root of . It is free of rank over the base, and the derivative is invertible because and are invertible. This gives étaleness, and faithful freeness of positive rank gives surjectivity on spectra. For the characteristic- map, the relative module of differentials contains the nonzero generator , since the derivative is zero. It is therefore not unramified.  "
